<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colonia Claudia Ara Agrippinensium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">50 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Colonia Agrippina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Colonia Claudia Ara Agrippinensium was the Roman city that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>. Founded on the site of the main settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubii">Ubii</a>, it received the rank of a colony in 50 CE under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> at the request of his wife Agrippina, who had been born there. It became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania-inferior">Germania Inferior</a> and one of the largest cities of the Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colonia-claudia-ara-agrippinensium.jpg" alt="Colonia Claudia Ara Agrippinensium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VollwertBIT · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roemerturm_Koeln2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
